  "brief": "<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Market Overview</h2>\n\nFutures pointing modestly higher with SPY up 0.25% to $756.48 as we close out what appears to be another record month. Tech is driving the bus with XLK up 2.23% pre-market while defensive sectors are getting sold. VIX down 1.71% to 24.14 suggests complacency is creeping back in despite elevated levels.\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> What to Watch</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Powell Speech (12:30 AM ET):</strong> Fed Chair kicks off the day with high-impact remarks that could shift rate expectations</li>\n<li><strong>Waller Speech (12:30 PM ET):</strong> Second Fed official speaking today - watch for hawkish/dovish divergence</li>\n<li><strong>Iran Tensions:</strong> Military blockade runner news could spike oil and defense stocks if situation escalates</li>\n<li><strong>Month-End Flows:</strong> Portfolio rebalancing could create unusual volume patterns across sectors</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Sector Rotation</h2>\n\nClear risk-on move with Tech leading (+2.23%) while defensive plays like Consumer Staples (-1.80%) and Utilities (-0.47%) get dumped. Energy weakness (-1.16%) despite Iran headlines suggests oversupply concerns still dominate. Small caps lagging hard with IWM down 0.55% - classic sign of selective buying in mega-cap growth.\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-green\"><div class=\"callout-label\">✦ Bull Case</div>Tech momentum accelerating into month-end with QQQ outperforming. VIX decline suggests fear subsiding and risk appetite returning for summer rally setup.</div>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-red\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚠ Bear Case</div>Small cap weakness and defensive sector selling could signal institutional distribution. Two Fed speakers today risk hawkish surprises that derail the party.</div>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-amber\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚡ Key Driver</div>Powell's tone on rate cuts will determine whether this tech rally has legs or runs into a Fed reality check.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Levels That Matter</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SPY $760:</strong> Monthly high resistance - break above confirms momentum continuation</li>\n<li><strong>QQQ $740:</strong> Round number resistance with tech leading the charge</li>\n<li><strong>VIX $22:</strong> Support level that signals return to low-vol regime</li>\n<li><strong>IWM $285:</strong> Critical support for small caps - breakdown warns of broader weakness</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr>\n<p><em>Not a prediction. A preparation. Make your plan before the bell.</em></p>",
